From 99f47f81802ddc33b6f58faf2ab74a53d431c999 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SquadronConsult <michael@defense-dna.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:12:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] board: ddna: add Shield SIL (emulated Shield, i.MX 8M Plus)

U-Boot proper for the Shield as emulated by the SIL's patched QEMU
imx8mp-evk machine: 4 GiB DRAM, eMMC on uSDHC3 (mmc 2) with the
environment in its boot1 area, console on UART2, FEC, watchdog. QEMU loads
TF-A and U-Boot, so there is no SPL and no binman image.

The watchdog is not started by U-Boot: under emulation, loading a large
kernel and initrd (Ubuntu) takes longer than its 60 s timeout before the
OS has a driver to feed it. The OS starts it (OpenWrt's procd).
